        "Abstract": "Commonsense reasoning is a critical component of any natural language understanding system. Contrary to textual entailment, commonsense reasoning must bridge between premises and possible hypotheses with world knowledge that is not explicit in text. We introduce XCOPA, a typologically diverse multilingual dataset for causal commonsense reasoning in 11 languages."
